# External libraries — what to use when

The office's `autocad-mcp` is glue, not a wheel-reinventing factory. When
the user asks for something that one of the libraries below already
solves, **prefer the library**. Each entry lists: install command, when
to use, gotchas, and the wrapper inside this repo.

## Quick decision matrix

| If the user asks for… | Use |
|---|---|
| Import blocks / layers / styles from another DWG | **Lee Mac `Steal.lsp`** + skill `steal-from-template` |
| Headless DWG/DXF batch ops (no AutoCAD running) | **ezdxf** + skill `dxf-headless-batch` |
| DXF/DWG → Shapefile / GeoPackage / EPSG reproj | **CAD_to_GIS** + skill `cad-to-gis` |
| Pythonic in-process AutoCAD scripting | **PyRx** (`pip install cad-pyrx`) |
| Drawing audit / fix proxies / dynamic-to-static | **FinalCAD/FINALCAD-CleanAndFix** (`FCCLEAN` cmd) |
| Plot generation / cadastre / urban routines | **vjspab/autocad-lisp-toolkit** |
| Wall centerline extraction from 2D plans | **beastt1992/WallCenterline** |
| Sun-path / insolation analysis (СНиП §6) | **FreeCAD Solar workbench** or **archilume** |
| IFC interop (BIM ↔ DWG) | **IfcOpenShell** + Bonsai Blender add-on |
| Pure-Rust DXF/DWG read/write | **acadrust**, **ezdwg** |

