## L01 — Lee Mac `Steal.lsp`

> The single most useful AutoLISP routine ever written.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Source | https://www.lee-mac.com/steal.html |
| License | Free (no resale; redistribution per author's terms) |
| Vendor location | `scripts/vendor/lee-mac/Steal.lsp` |
| Wrapper | `scripts/utilities/steal-from-template.lsp` |
| Skill | `.cursor/skills/steal-from-template/` |

Imports any combination of *blocks, layers, linetypes, dim styles, text
styles, table styles, MLeader styles, layouts, page setups, groups,
materials, multileader styles* from one DWG to another. Use this every
time we set up a new project from a reference DWG in
`wetransfer_03_xref_saproeqto_*` or `wetransfer_19_xref_grg_*`.

Variants:

- `Steal` — interactive picker
- `StealAll` — grab everything
- `StealLast` — re-uses the last source DWG
- `StealTemplate` / `StealTemplates` — pulls from `.dwt`

**Gotcha:** Steal.lsp is **not on GitHub**; it must be downloaded and
placed manually at `scripts/vendor/lee-mac/Steal.lsp`. See
`scripts/vendor/README.md`.

