## L03 — CAD_to_GIS (we use **fiona**, not raw GDAL)

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Source (inspiration) | https://github.com/skyflying/CAD_to_GIS |
| QGIS plugin | https://github.com/skyflying/CAD_to_GIS_QGIS_Plugin |
| License | MIT |
| Install (Python) | `pip install -r requirements.txt` |
| Wrapper | `scripts/python/cad_to_gis.py` |
| Skill | `.cursor/skills/cad-to-gis/` |

Converts DXF (and DWG via auto-conversion) layers to **GeoJSON** (default),
ESRI Shapefile, or single-layer GeoPackage with EPSG reprojection.
Implemented with **fiona + shapely + pyproj** because raw GDAL bindings
are a pain on Windows / Python 3.12 — fiona ships its own GDAL build.

Use when:

- The user needs `xref_sakutreba.dwg` in QGIS.
- Cadastre layers must go to the gov GIS (EPSG:32638 for Tbilisi).
- We want polygon attributes from MText labels.

Output is **one file per CAD layer**. To merge into a single multi-layer
GeoPackage, run `ogrmerge.py -f GPKG -single -o all.gpkg out/*.gpkg`.

**Gotchas:**
- Block references are exploded by ezdxf before geometry conversion.
- 3D polylines flatten to 2D — losing Z.
- GPKG multi-layer single-file mode hits a fiona NULL-pointer bug on
  Windows; we work around by writing one `.gpkg` per layer.

