## House rules for using external libraries

1. **License hygiene.** Always note the license in the vendor README
   and at the top of each adapter. GPL libs (LibreDWG) cannot be
   shipped inside proprietary plugins.
2. **Version pin.** Pin every Python lib in `requirements.txt`
   (`ezdxf==1.4.4`, `cad-pyrx==2.2.50`, etc.).
3. **One adapter per library**, never call the lib directly from the
   MCP server. Adapters live in `scripts/python/` or
   `scripts/utilities/` and expose a single CLI / `c:` entry point.
4. **Vendored LSPs** go to `scripts/vendor/<author>/<file>.lsp` and are
   `git`-ignored if the license forbids redistribution.
5. **Skills wrap adapters.** Every adapter has a matching skill at
   `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` with a workflow checklist and
   pitfalls.
